        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4aa6f732bd794455957bca6d0ead825b",
      "statement": "FrozenArmMixin.state_dict strips the registered frozen arms in place on the caller-supplied destination and is prefix-aware, so the arms are excluded from the checkpoint and cannot leak under a DDP wrapper prefix (module.frozen.*).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L82-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19414104e9bdf43116dce701b0afa36a6380b2553b09a125335ff357101a56ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8004b6cf00ed4a31a4f1869df0f84428",
      "statement": "FrozenArmMixin.load_state_dict is strict on the trainable keys with the frozen arms as an explicit allow-list: stray frozen keys are dropped from the incoming mapping, super() is called with strict=False, and any non-frozen missing or unexpected key raises a RuntimeError — deliberately not a blanket strict=False that would resume on stale or random weights.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L107-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01d618e345d65323ff4304bbfcc9aee0057c937522aafc8fdcbc847717b4cf43:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fd25da9a8c81475bbc4c3f7aa4e3f6d7",
      "statement": "FrozenArmMixin.train(mode) re-applies eval() to every registered frozen arm after super().train(mode), undoing the training-mode flip that registration causes so a frozen arm's BatchNorm running stats cannot drift during rollout or reward evaluation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L139-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d9b2d8864c5dfb4e0d51c3bc39792d5165c79e8445b6d2ab672d38d101d60c11:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cd8bf0c4271841d78714dba609ecbc36",
      "statement": "The mixin does NOT own optimizer arm-selection: each host's configure_optimizers wires only its trainable arm (GRPOModule selects the unet on the UNet policy or the controlnet on the ControlNet policy, RewardModule selects reward_model, ControlNetLatentFlowModule selects controlnet), and the mixin guarantees only the requires_grad=False layer.",
      "evidence": [
