    {
      "id": "claim_f064a4fdedb440d098edce8075be983b",
      "statement": "The GRPO base freeze is a derived invariant rather than a constructor argument: the presence of a ControlNet turns the policy UNet into the frozen base, so on the UNet-policy path the same `unet` is the trainable policy and is deliberately never registered as a frozen arm; when no KL reference is supplied the reference arms stay plain None attributes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/grpo.py#L346-L359",
