    {
      "id": "claim_2ac9fcd458be4d96975b34abb232b773",
      "statement": "Registering the frozen arms carries a documented DDP-init broadcast cost: at DistributedDataParallel construction every registered parameter, including the requires_grad=False frozen arms, is synchronized from rank 0 (a one-time startup cost, not per-step), and the mitigation is to construct the arms on each rank from the same source rather than adding a DDP exclusion hack.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0031-device-ownership.md#L152-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38529b393a4b56bf770f490326a64c26ce47cb759426e8d295d56c1e7f204e60:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6397d25277fd4eba850ea26f6189685f",
      "statement": "The off-checkpoint invariant reaches the export bridge: a supervised-ControlNet checkpoint carries only the trainable `controlnet.*` keys because the frozen base contributes no `unet.unet.*` keys, which is exactly the precondition export_to_native requires to bake a ControlNet export (although its comment still describes the retired object.__setattr__ mechanism).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/export.py#L26-L31",
